\begin{abstract}
This paper presents the scientific testing suite for the Unified Quantum-Gravitational
Simulation Engine (UQG-SE v1.0). The system integrates LQG spin-network geometry,
string-theoretic excitations, relativistic Dirac-Fock solvers, encrypted multi-messenger
telemetry, and autonomous damping control. Numerical stability, solver fidelity,
cryptographic performance, and convergence to the Universal Stability threshold
$\sigma = 10^{-8}$ are reported.
\end{abstract}

